        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-13T13:59:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "A while back I filed b/388497880 to handle this case and just convert it to a `SolidColor` on the CPU.  This is either an FYI it\u0027ll change later, or a \"should we prioritize getting that through the door if it\u0027s not too hard?\"",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 77,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 77,
        "endChar": 93
      },
      "revId": "06838ed7b10dc93b712a22d07e90b7f174dab2c8",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a61b658a_3db7d322",
        "filename": "tests/graphite/precompile/ChromePrecompileTest.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 77,
      "author": {
        "id": 5230
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-13T14:23:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That would be great! I fully expect we\u0027ll have to update these regularly, based on UMA stats feedback, so I\u0027m inclined to just let things ride for now.",
      "parentUuid": "2d5dbc6d_2602b2bf",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 77,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 77,
        "endChar": 93
      },
      "revId": "06838ed7b10dc93b712a22d07e90b7f174dab2c8",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "20c0cac2_798c34a3",
        "filename": "tests/graphite/precompile/ChromePrecompileTest.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 413,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-13T13:59:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is an open question about how we want to handle analytic clipping and clip shaders with precompilation. We could always combine them w/ overgeneration, we could require that they include clip options X paint options, or we could ignore them entirely and just trigger on-the-fly compilation.\n\nWhen we have a low priority background thread, handling the analytic clip overgeneration is probably acceptable.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 413,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 413,
        "endChar": 70
      },
      "revId": "06838ed7b10dc93b712a22d07e90b7f174dab2c8",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "967078f1_8565892e",
        "filename": "tests/graphite/precompile/ChromePrecompileTest.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 10
      },
      "lineNbr": 413,
      "author": {
        "id": 5230
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-03-13T14:23:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah - I suspect there will be some cases we\u0027ll want to Precompile but I\u0027m a bit skeptical re the generality of the Chrome stories used to generate this set. Regardless of how we express it in the Precompile API I would like to get some actual UMA stats to guide which AnalyticClip Pipelines we generate.",
      "parentUuid": "20c0cac2_798c34a3",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 413,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 413,
        "endChar": 70
      },
